"# Release Policy\n"
"\n"
"This document describes the release policy for the project, including version numbering, release cadence, and support lifecycle.\n"
"\n"
"## Version Numbering\n"
"\n"
"The project follows Semantic Versioning (SemVer). Version numbers are structured as `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`:\n"
"\n"
"- **MAJOR**: Incremented for incompatible API changes.\n"
"- **MINOR**: Incremented for backward-compatible functionality additions.\n"
"- **PATCH**: Incremented for backward-compatible bug fixes.\n"
"\n"
"Pre-release versions may be denoted with suffixes such as `-alpha`, `-beta`, or `-rc`.\n"
"\n"
"## Release Cadence\n"
"\n"
"- **Major Releases**: Scheduled annually, may include breaking changes.\n"
"- **Minor Releases**: Scheduled quarterly, add features in a backward-compatible manner.\n"
"- **Patch Releases**: Released as needed to address critical bug fixes and security vulnerabilities.\n"
"\n"
"## Support Lifecycle\n"
"\n"
"- **Active Support**: The latest minor version of the current major release receives full support, including bug fixes and security patches.\n"
"- **Maintenance Support**: The previous major release receives security patches for a defined period after a new major release.\n"
"- **End of Life (EOL)**: Releases that have reached EOL no longer receive updates or support.\n"
"\n"
"## Release Process\n"
"\n"
"1. **Development**: All changes are merged into the main branch.\n"
"2. **Release Candidate**: A release candidate branch is created, and testing is conducted.\n"
"3. **Stable Release**: After validation, the release candidate is tagged and published.\n"
"4. **Post-Release**: Patch releases are created from the release branch as needed.\n"
"\n"
"## Backporting\n"
"\n"
"Critical bug fixes and security patches may be backported to supported release branches at the maintainers' discretion.\n"
"\n"
"## Deprecation Policy\n"
"\n"
"Deprecated features are announced in the release notes and remain functional for at least one minor release before removal.\n"

